---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hud from "../components/Hud.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_NAME, SOCIAL } from "../consts";

const title = `Terms of Service | ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description = `Terms of Service of ${SITE_NAME}: the agreement covering use of this site and its content.`;
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Hud />
  <main class="doc">
    <div class="shell">
      <article class="panel panel--riveted doc__panel">
        <p class="stencil">terms of service</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="doc__stamp">Last updated: October 23, 2026</p>

        <div class="doc__body">
          <section>
            <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
            <p>
              Welcome to {SITE_NAME} (the "Site"). By accessing or using the Site you agree
              to be bound by these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>2. Site Content</h2>
            <p>
              Content on the Site is provided "as is" for product-family introduction and
              build-in-public status purposes and may change as the effort evolves. We
              strive for accuracy but make no express or implied warranties regarding
              completeness or timeliness.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>3. Working Name and Availability</h2>
            <p>
              "Tier 0" is a working name. The system described is a milestone-based work in
              progress: as of the revision date, the M0–M4 gates have passed, while the
              system is not operable as a business before M8. Live sales channels, payment,
              store-entity qualifications and durable persistence are explicitly pending and
              are presented as fail-closed or placeholder states. Nothing here constitutes a
              commitment to ship a specific feature or on a specific date.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>4. Illustrative Figures</h2>
            <p>
              Test counts, identifiers, status codes, error codes, milestone names and the
              status board shown on the Site are dated build snapshots used to document the
              engineering state. They are not real transactions, not benchmarks and do not
              represent the performance of any real workload.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>5. Intellectual Property</h2>
            <p>
              The Site's copy, design and branding belong to the project team and may not be
              used commercially without permission. The software and its source code are
              governed by the license declared in their respective repositories.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>6. Acceptable Use</h2>
            <p>
              Do not use the Site in ways that could harm or disrupt its operation or
              infringe on others' rights, including malicious scraping, injection attacks,
              or impersonation of the Site.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
            <p>
              To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Site is not liable for any
              indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from use of or inability
              to use its content. You are responsible for how you operate any of the
              software and how you connect it to live channels.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>8. Changes</h2>
            <p>
              These terms may be updated; changes will be posted on this page. Continued use
              of the Site constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>9. Contact</h2>
            <p>
              Questions about these terms can be raised via Issues on our
              <a href={SOCIAL.github}>GitHub repository</a>, or by email at
              <a href={`mailto:${SOCIAL.email}`}>{SOCIAL.email}</a>.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <a class="btn btn--ghost doc__back" href="/">Back to console</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
